# Named Dockerfile.dockerignore (not plain .dockerignore), colocated with
# the Dockerfile it applies to -- Docker/BuildKit looks for a
# "<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore" next to the Dockerfile first, before
# falling back to a plain .dockerignore at the build context root. Build
# context here is the repo root (see Dockerfile's header comment), so a
# plain .dockerignore would have had to live there instead, one level
# above where the rest of this project's Docker-specific files live -- this
# naming keeps everything Docker-related inside this one folder.
# If your Docker version predates this lookup (BuildKit, default since
# Docker 23.0), copy this file's contents into a plain .dockerignore at the
# repo root instead -- see Docker/README.md.
.git
.github
.vscode
.claude
ESP32
Drawings
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/filters.json
